  "title": "MP-02 F3: V2 admission from bytes under dcp-jcs-v1",
  "status": "Opt-in route admitSignedBundleV2FromBytes. dcp-jcs-v1, the candidate dcp-jcs-v2, the profiles and the defaults are unchanged.",
  "date": "07/11/2026",
  "design": "docs/reviews/mp02-security-composition-design.md section 3; .claude/handoff/INFORME-CODEX-MP02-F3-DISENO.md",
  "generated_by": ".claude/mp02-20261107/claude-f3/gen_v1_ingress_vectors.py (data only; no SDK)",
  "how_to_read": {
    "route": "Private copy of the bytes; the candidate scanner unchanged (layer scanner); the portable integer domain over number literals outside strings (layer domain); the concrete parser, canonicalized with dcp-jcs-v1 and compared byte for byte with the scanner canonical (layer parser, class INGRESS_PARSER_MISMATCH, offset null); then admitSignedBundleV2 over that parsed value.",
    "domain": "A number literal outside strings must match -?(0|[1-9][0-9]*) and must not be -0. Range is the scanner's. Offset is the literal's first byte in the unit.",
    "sources": "Every document/bare unit of the two corpora keeps its own expectation, read from the pinned file: a scanner rejection with its class and offset, or acceptance with its canonical_sha256. The exceptions are the domain_differences.",
    "admission": "None of these units is a signed bundle: every accepted unit must reach admission and be neither verified nor admitted."
  },
